-dui-college-students-struck-highway/73446950", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "17-year-old {  Mauricio Palafox-Correa}    charged with DUI after two SC college students hit while crossing highway {he actuall killed at least two and also a third later after fleeing the scene}", "last_comment_created": 1787493329157, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 3, "score_up": 21, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "Two SC college students were struck by a teen driver who was later charged with driving under the influence, officials say.", "large_image": "zYHfsxrnbPidgMXy.png", "title": "Teen charged with DUI after SC college students hit while crossing highway"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATCNSkdVf", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 14, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8794617, "raw_content": "*On August 15, 1971, Richard Nixon interrupted Sunday-night television to announce the New Economic Policy*. \r\n\r\n*With the Vietnam War winding down, Nixon argued, the economy required federal action to deliver what he called \u201ca new prosperity without war.\u201d Nixon declared that night, \u201cWe must create more and better jobs; we must stop the rise in the cost of living; we must protect the dollar from the attacks of international money speculators.\u201d*\r\n\r\nThose days had some unique problems - but losing gold opened the pandora's box of Printing and Borrowing... I don't know if Nixon really saw that coming. \r\n\r\nhttps://thedailyeconomy.org/article/the-lesson-of-1971-was-never-about-gold/", "author": "Bullet3250", "created": 1787495250598, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Bullet3250", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "55 years ago, August 15th, - President Nixon removes the Dollar from the Gold standard.  More to it than just paper. ", "last_comment_created": 1787501597354, "content": "<p><em>On August 15, 1971, Richard Nixon interrupted Sunday-night television to announce the New Economic Policy</em>.</p>\n<p><em>With the Vietnam War winding down, Nixon argued, the economy required federal action to deliver what he called \u201ca new prosperity without war.\u201d Nixon declared that night, \u201cWe must create more and better jobs; we must stop the rise in the cost of living; we must protect the dollar from the attacks of international money speculators.\u201d</em></p>\n<p>Those days had some unique problems - but losing gold opened the pandora's box of Printing and Borrowing... I don't know if Nixon really saw that coming.</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://thedailyeconomy.org/article/the-lesson-of-1971-was-never-about-gold/\" target=\"_blank\">https://thedailyeconomy.org/article/the-lesson-of-1971-was-never-about-gold/</a></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 9, "score_up": 14, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATCNSkMSX", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 18, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8794511, "raw